// src/lsp/lsp.zen
// The language server, and the folder's surface.
//
// Graded against `PLAN.md` stage 4 and `docs/design_lsp.md`. `DESIGN.md:45`:
// the LSP is "a thin server over compiler internals" — nothing here may
// answer a question about Zen itself; a missing query belongs in
// `src/sema/` or `src/ast/`.
//
// A folder root is starred re-exports only; an absent name is
// module-private.
//
//   lsp_pos.zen        the wire's coordinates and this language's
//   lsp_json.zen       JSON as a value, an arena, and the writer
//   lsp_json_read.zen  JSON in
//   lsp_frame.zen      Content-Length framing
//   lsp_decl.zen       which declared name a position is inside
//   lsp_uri.zen        a document URI, as a path the compiler can open
//   lsp_hover.zen      the one query wired to sema
//   lsp_colour.zen     semanticTokens: colour, from the lexer, and from
//                      the checker where it settled a name
//   lsp_names.zen      the semantic half: which names a clean build
//                      settled, read off the checker's memos
//   lsp_diag.zen       publishDiagnostics: the build, grouped by file
//   lsp_serve.zen      lifecycle, the overlay, and the dispatch table
//   lsp_stdio.zen      the pipe: frames in on stdin, frames out on stdout
//
// BUILT: L1 whole (transport, lifecycle, sync, diagnostics) plus TWO
// queries — hover and semanticTokens/full — over stdio via `zen lsp`.
// Everything else in `design_lsp.md` §2's table is refused with `-32601`.
//
// Hover and diagnostics need a build (root, disk, a `Checker`, ~1s) and
// go quiet without one. Colour's LEXICAL half needs only a `scan`, so it
// answers on an unsaved buffer with no workspace, even on a file that
// does not parse — why VS Code gets colour from this server at all. The
// SEMANTIC half (L4) rides the diagnostics' build: with no workspace, a
// change not yet settled, or a program with faults, the answer degrades
// to lexical and never to grey.
//
// Diagnostics are all three phases or nothing: lex/parse (on `Build`) go
// out beside sema (on `Checker`), so type errors never show while syntax
// errors go unreported.
//
// NOT BUILT: documentSymbol, definition, references, completion,
// formatting, signatureHelp, rename (L2-L4); semanticTokens' `range` and
// `full/delta` shapes, deliberately not advertised (`design_lsp.md` §2).

WirePos*, LineRun*, Step*, to_pos*, to_wire*, run_of*, step_at* = lsp.lsp_pos
write_wire*, write_range*, wire_at*, units_of* = lsp.lsp_pos
JsonId*, Run*, Pair*, Json*, Jsons*, write_text*, whole_of* = lsp.lsp_json
JsonFault*, Reader*, read*, push_utf8*, byte_of* = lsp.lsp_json_read
Envelope*, FrameFault*, frame_at*, write_frame*, write_decimal* = lsp.lsp_frame
short_by* = lsp.lsp_frame
Tell*, TypeAt*, ValueAt*, told_at*, is_nothing* = lsp.lsp_decl
Hover*, hover_at*, hover_in*, no_type* = lsp.lsp_hover
FILE_SCHEME*, path_of*, uri_at* = lsp.lsp_uri
Spot*, Diagnostics*, found_in*, publish*, ERROR* = lsp.lsp_diag
Colour*, Classed*, index_of*, name_of*, colour_of* = lsp.lsp_colour
write_legend*, write_tokens*, sort_classes* = lsp.lsp_colour
classify* = lsp.lsp_names
Server*, serve*, write_capabilities*, SEMANTIC_TOKENS* = lsp.lsp_serve
frame_byte*, frame_why* = lsp.lsp_serve
Drain*, serve_stdio* = lsp.lsp_stdio
